# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build context for docker/Dockerfile (the Python backend image).
# Its build context is the repo root, and the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so
# anything not excluded here is baked into the image. Keep this list tight:
#   - SECURITY: secrets (.env), git history, and local venvs must never ship.
#   - SIZE: the Next.js admin panel, node_modules, caches, and data are huge and
#     the backend image does not need them.
# What the backend runtime DOES need (do NOT ignore): app/, migrations/,
# alembic.ini, requirements.txt, docker/, main_polling.py, scripts/, pyproject.toml
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets & environment ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Version control ──
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Python virtualenvs (local, wrong platform/version for the image) ──
.venv/
venv/

# ── Python caches / build artifacts ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/

# ── The admin panel is a SEPARATE image (admin-panel/Dockerfile); the ──
# ── backend does not need any of it, least of all its node_modules. ──
admin-panel/

# ── Runtime data (bind-mounted at ./data:/app/data; never bake it in) ──
data/

# ── Tests (not needed in the production image) ──
tests/

# ── Docs & scratch files ──
*.md
!README.md
adminpanel.md
ADMIN_SETTINGS_AUDIT.md
setup-guild.txt
test-phases.txt

# ── Logs & editor/OS cruft ──
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Other compose files not part of this image build ──
docker-compose.dev.yml
docker-compose.admin.yml
